    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4d677a72",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: trump-bully-meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts Donald Trump pointing aggressively, with text overlay stating 'he is proving that grown adults can be a bully.' The scene uses Trump's recognizable image and confrontational gesture to convey a judgmental message about his behavior. The intent is to criticize and label Trump as a bully, which can be seen as harmful as it contributes to a negative public perception of him and may incite division or hostility. While not explicitly targeting a protected group, the meme promotes a negative characterization of a public figure, which can influence public opinion and potentially harm his reputation or political standing. The overall intent is to discredit or delegitimize Trump by associating him with bullying behavior, using visual and textual juxtaposition to reinforce this judgment.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f988b201"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
